            "topic_title": "Getting started"
          }
        },
        "q_what_is": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What is Threaditate?",
            "answer": "<p>Threaditate turns a photo you love into string art you make by hand. You upload the photo to the app, it converts it into a numbered pattern, and you follow that pattern thread by thread on a 20-inch loom until your picture appears. No experience needed. Everything — the loom, the thread, and the app — ships in one box.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q_any_photo": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can I use any photo?",
            "answer": "<p>Almost any photo works. Portraits and close-ups with clear contrast tend to come out best — the app reads light and shadow rather than fine detail. A favorite person, a pet, a place that means something to you. Upload it, and the app does the rest.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q_experience": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Do I need any experience?",
            "answer": "<p>None. The app walks you through every step, one thread at a time. There's nothing to figure out on your own, and nothing to memorize. The first step is the same for everyone — the app accounts for the rest.</p>"
          }
        },
        "topic_the_kit": {
          "type": "topic_header",
          "settings": {
            "topic_title": "The kit"
          }
        },
        "q_whats_in_kit": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What's in the kit?",
            "answer": "<p>Your kit comes with a 20-inch birch loom set with 240 pins, thread, and free access to the Threaditate app. Open the box and you have everything you need to start the same day.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q_need_app": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Do I need the app?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes — and it's free. The app is what makes Threaditate guided. Without it, you have string art. With it, you have a session: real-time instructions, one step at a time, on iPhone and Android. Access is included with every kit.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q_other_tools": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Do I need any other tools or supplies?",
            "answer": "<p>Nothing extra. The loom, the pins, the thread, and the app are all you need. Set aside a comfortable spot with good light, and you're ready to begin.</p>"
          }
        },
        "topic_the_process": {
          "type": "topic_header",
          "settings": {
            "topic_title": "The process"
          }
        },
        "q_how_long": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How long does it take?",
            "answer": "<p>Most pieces take between 45 minutes and three hours, depending on the photo. There's no clock, and you don't have to finish in one sitting. The app saves your place after every thread, so you can take it at your own pace.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q_lose_place": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What if I lose my place?",
            "answer": "<p>The app remembers exactly where you stopped, down to the last thread you confirmed. Step away for an hour or a week, then pick up right where you left off.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q_mistake": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What if I make a mistake?",
            "answer": "<p>Pick up from your last confirmed step and keep going. Small slips vanish in the finished piece — your eye reads the whole image, not individual threads. The design is more forgiving than you think.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q_thread_breaks": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What if the thread breaks?",
            "answer": "<p>It rarely happens, but if it does, tie the two ends together in a small knot and keep going. The knot tucks behind the pins and won't show in your finished piece.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q_warping": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Will the loom warp?",
            "answer": "<p>Only if the thread is wound too tight. Keep a light, even tension as you go and your 20-inch loom stays flat. If you've been pulling hard and notice a slight bow, ease off and it usually settles back. A relaxed hand is all it takes.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q_pause": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can I pause and come back to it?",
            "answer": "<p>Anytime. The app holds your progress automatically, so a Threaditate fits around your life. Some people finish in an afternoon. Others thread a little each evening over a week.</p>"
          }
        },
        "topic_after_finish": {
          "type": "topic_header",
          "settings": {
            "topic_title": "After you finish"
          }
        },
        "q_display": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How do I display my finished piece?",
            "answer": "<p>Your finished piece is made to be seen. The 20-inch loom hangs flat on a standard picture nail, sits on a shelf, or rests on an easel — no frame needed. Find a spot with good light and it will stop people in their tracks.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q_reuse": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can I make a new piece with the same loom?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. When you're ready for a new picture, remove the thread and start fresh with a new pattern on the same loom. Each loom holds one piece at a time, so to make several at once, simply add more kits.</p>"
          }
        },
